{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Design notes (2026-11-21 PST, origin/main 863abe7cd19). Census of the 56 lines (23 modules): 15 modules write '#!/bin/sh' stub executables onto PATH, 6 run bash/sh/make directly, test_repo_isolation_guard writes '#!{sys.executable}' scripts, and test_metrics_polyglot / test_serena_grep_reminder_hook / test_check_readme_quickstart / test_repair_pause_ownership_store use other spawn paths, each needing a per-module read. Why the stubs never run: subprocess on Windows calls CreateProcess, which looks up a bare name like 'git' on PATH by appending '.exe' only. It ignores PATHEXT, so neither a shebang file nor a 'git.cmd' shim can shadow git.exe. And 'bash' on the runner's PATH resolves to the WSL launcher (UTF-16 'no installed distributions' output in test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew / test_predates_gate_guard_parity). Proposed class fix: one test helper (tests/_exe_stub.py) installing a stub whose body is Python. On POSIX it writes a '#!{sys.executable}' script with mode 0755; on Windows it builds a real '<name>.exe' with distlib's ScriptMaker launcher (t64.exe / t64-arm.exe, shipped in distlib 0.4.3, which uv.lock already resolves via virtualenv), so CreateProcess finds it. Each module's sh stub body is ported to Python against the helper. Tests whose subject is a POSIX shell recipe (make worktree, bash-gate parity, shellcheck) get a Windows skip with the reason, which the AC allows. distlib is only a transitive dependency today; the change would declare it in the dev extra rather than rely on virtualenv. Validation: a tmp-branch Windows run of the tree with the fixed lines removed from posix-shell-stubs.args."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795255840699105001,"uuid":"6837185c-99ef-4831-84a0-aba7522210da"}